{"sections": [
  {"key": "arc", "title": "The arc", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue compounded at 26.0% a year from $4.32 billion in FY2016 to $34.6 billion in FY2025 [F1][F10][F231]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The path was a step change, not a straight line: revenue rose 68.3% in FY2021 and 43.6% in FY2022, then fell 3.9% in FY2023 before recovering 13.7% and 34.3% [D258][D314][D370][D426][D483]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2022 jump included the Xilinx acquisition, which added Embedded revenue of $4.55 billion against $246 million a year earlier [S110][S109][P41]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2023 decline came from a 25% drop in Client revenue on weak PC demand and inventory correction, partly offset by Embedded [P35]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Data Center revenue reached $16.6 billion in FY2025, 48.0% of total revenue, and contributed 15.7pp of the 34.3% growth [S98][D692][D694][D483]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The filing attributes that growth to strong demand for 5th generation AMD EPYC processors and AMD Instinct MI350 Series GPUs [P15]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Client and Gaming added 19.0pp, with Client revenue of $10.6 billion up 51% on a 31% rise in processor units and a 15% rise in average selling price [D701][S124][P10]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating income grew 94.4% against 34.3% revenue growth, an incremental operating margin of 20.3% [D484][D483][D511]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Diluted EPS rose 165.0% against 164.2% net income growth, as the diluted share count was flat at -0.1% [D487][D485][D506]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "margins", "title": "Margins and costs", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Gross margin of 49.5% is the window high, against a 44.7% median [F40][D800][D801]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating margin of 10.7% sits above the 7.2% window median but far below the 22.2% FY2021 high [F60][D795][D794]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "In FY2025 cost of revenue added only 0.2pp while SG&A subtracted 1.2pp and R&D added 1.7pp [D513][D515][D514]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Gross margin improved on product mix, partly offset by about $440 million of MI308 inventory and related charges tied to U.S. export controls [P14]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Net margin of 12.5% exceeded operating margin by 1.9pp, helped by $577 million of other income from unrealized investment gains and a $103 million tax benefit [F80][F60][D843][P5][P4]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "cash", "title": "Cash conversion", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Operating cash flow was $7.71 billion and free cash flow $6.74 billion in FY2025, a 19.4% free-cash-flow margin [F110][F130][D467]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow was 1.55x net income against a 1.17x window median [D471][D810]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Operating cash flow was reduced by a $2.2 billion inventory build to support the Data Center ramp [P3]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Capex of $974 million was 2.8% of revenue and 1.87x D&A, the highest ratio in the window [F120][D466][D472]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "balance_sheet", "title": "Balance sheet and capital allocation", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Cash and investments of $10.6 billion against $4.10 billion of debt left net cash of $6.46 billion, 18.6% of revenue [D474][D475][D476][D477]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "That net cash position ranks at the 100th percentile of five semis peers, whose median is -17.3% of revenue [D844][D845]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Debt rose 138% to $4.10 billion, including $1.5 billion of notes issued in March 2025 [D508][D475][P6]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Buybacks of $1.32 billion were 19.5% of free cash flow, and the diluted share count was flat [X150][D479][D506]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "red_flags", "title": "Red flags", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue fell 3.9% in FY2023, the only decline in the window, driven by Client and Gaming weakness [D370][P35]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Total debt rose 138% in FY2025 to $4.10 billion, though net cash still rose to $6.46 billion [D508][D475][D476]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "The effective tax rate moved -21.3pp to -2.5% on an $853 million uncertain-tax-position release, so the FY2025 net margin is not a clean run rate [D469][D412][P4]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Days inventory outstanding rose to 165 days from 160, extending a climb from 106 days in FY2022 [D481][D424][D312]."}
